Seeded mutation fuzzing over the two of roadmap section 7's four surfaces that exist:
the verifier, and the executor over verified-but-adversarial artifacts. The source
tokenizer and parser and the regular-expression matcher are surfaces this profile has
not written, and a session may not be read as covering them.

ANSWER-GUIDED, AND NOT COVERAGE-GUIDED. The adjective is the whole of the claim. A
mutant whose published answer no seed artifact produces is kept as a further seed; the
pool opens as the retained corpus and grows to a ceiling. Each session reports what it
did: how many answers the seeds reached, how many the session ended on, how many mutants
it kept, and the pool size before and after.

WHAT THAT IS NOT. The signal is the answer this profile PUBLISHES, not an edge the
mutant executed. Two paths to one answer are one signal, and a defect on a path that
answers like its neighbour is invisible to the guidance. Instrumenting for anything
finer would put a coverage host in a published closure or change the assembly under
test, and JSD-0013 records that refusal and what would falsify it.

THIS HEADER HAS BEEN WRONG BEFORE, IN BOTH DIRECTIONS. It said coverage-guided when the
mutator took no feedback at all, which JSC-38 corrected to NOT coverage-guided. It then
said no session takes feedback after the sessions began taking it. The precise claim is
the one above: feedback by published answer, and no edge coverage anywhere.

Each session is a total function of its seed and the seed corpus. A session that answers
the same way every time, or that never reaches the executor, exits NON-ZERO rather than
reporting clean iterations it did not earn.

